  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "Another half-angle formula for the tangent function can be found using the figure below, in which $\\triangle ABC$ is inscribed in a unit circle with centre $O$. Suppose $\\angle BAC=\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q23-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 8 p8-q23-diagram\"}\n\\usetikzlibrary{calc,angles,quotes}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.7cm,y=2.7cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},line cap=round,line join=round]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (A) at (-1,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (1,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at ({cos(52)},{sin(52)});\n\\coordinate (D) at (B |- O);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (O) circle (1);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (A)--(C) (A)--(B)--(C) (O)--(B) (B)--(D);\n\\coordinate (Rup) at ($(D)!0.11!(B)$);\n\\coordinate (Rright) at ($(D)!0.11!(C)$);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (Rup)--($(Rup)+(Rright)-(D)$)--(Rright);\n\\path (A)--(O) node[midway,below] {$1$};\n\\pic[draw=none,angle radius=17mm,angle eccentricity=1,\"$\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$\"] {angle=C--A--B};\n\\node[left] at (A) {$A$};\n\\node[below] at (O) {$O$};\n\\node[below] at (D) {$D$};\n\\node[right] at (C) {$C$};\n\\node[above] at (B) {$B$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 49,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 8,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 23, lower left column",
          "description": "Unshaded unit circle with diameter AC, centre O, upper-right point B and perpendicular BD. Includes chords AB and BC, radius OB, AO=1 and the angle BAC label. Coordinates select a representative view without adding numerical givens.",
          "mathematics": "A, O, D and C are collinear in that order; B lies on the unit circle; BD is perpendicular to AC; angle BAC is alpha/2.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only source givens are visible; OD, DB and angle BOD remain unlabelled."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q23-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $\\angle BOD$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha$",
          "worked": "The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference subtending arc $BC$. Since $OD$ lies along $OC$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle BOD&=2\\angle BAC\\\\\\angle BOD&=2\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)\\\\\\angle BOD&=\\alpha.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find lengths $OD$ and $DB$ in terms of $\\alpha$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$OD=\\cos\\alpha$, $DB=\\sin\\alpha$",
          "worked": "In right-angled triangle $ODB$, $OB=1$ and $\\angle BOD=\\alpha$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\alpha&=\\frac{OD}{1}\\\\OD&=\\cos\\alpha\\\\\\sin\\alpha&=\\frac{DB}{1}\\\\DB&=\\sin\\alpha.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q23-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that\n$$\\tan\\frac{\\alpha}{2}=\\frac{\\sin\\alpha}{1+\\cos\\alpha}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}=\\dfrac{\\sin\\alpha}{1+\\cos\\alpha}$\n\nUse $\\tan\\angle BAD=\\frac{DB}{AD}$ and $AD=AO+OD$.",
          "worked": "In right-angled triangle $ABD$, $\\angle BAD=\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\frac{\\alpha}{2}&=\\frac{DB}{AD}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\alpha}{2}&=\\frac{DB}{AO+OD}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\alpha}{2}&=\\frac{\\sin\\alpha}{1+\\cos\\alpha}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q23-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Using triangle $CBD$, also deduce that\n$$\\tan\\frac{\\alpha}{2}=\\frac{1-\\cos\\alpha}{\\sin\\alpha}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}=\\dfrac{1-\\cos\\alpha}{\\sin\\alpha}$\n\nUse $\\angle CBD=\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$, $CD=1-\\cos\\alpha$ and $BD=\\sin\\alpha$.",
          "worked": "Since $AC$ is a diameter, $\\angle ABC=90^\\circ$. In right-angled triangle $ABD$, $\\angle ABD=90^\\circ-\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$, so $\\angle CBD=\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}CD&=OC-OD\\\\CD&=1-\\cos\\alpha\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\alpha}{2}&=\\frac{CD}{BD}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\alpha}{2}&=\\frac{1-\\cos\\alpha}{\\sin\\alpha}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q23-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "What do you obtain if you multiply the above two identities?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan^2\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}=\\dfrac{1-\\cos\\alpha}{1+\\cos\\alpha}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan^2\\frac{\\alpha}{2}&=\\frac{\\sin\\alpha}{1+\\cos\\alpha}\\cdot\\frac{1-\\cos\\alpha}{\\sin\\alpha}\\\\\\tan^2\\frac{\\alpha}{2}&=\\frac{1-\\cos\\alpha}{1+\\cos\\alpha}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
